  "description": "Color silkscreen poster by artist Richard Halls for the Federal Theatre Project’s presentation of Theodore Pratt’s “Big Blow” at Maxine Elliott’s Theatre in New York City. The catalog describes a woman and a man struggling against gale-force winds. Dated between 1936 and 1939, with a June 28, 1939 stamp noted on the verso. The Federal Theatre Project is identified as sponsor.",
